<title>USA: Copper stocks outside U.S. up in August - ABMS.</title>
<headline>Copper stocks outside U.S. up in August - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refined copper stocks held by refineries outside the United States rose to 772,400 short tons at the end of August from a revised 762,700 short tons at the end of July, said the American Bureau of Metal Statistics.</p>
<p>London Metal Exchange stocks rose to 303,400 short tons in August from July's tally of 250,600 short tons.</p>
<p>Total refined copper stocks outside the U.S. rose to 1,075,800 short tons in August from a revised 1,013,300 short tons for the previous month.</p>
<p>--New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
